{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Notebook: Asistente Turístico (RAG mínimo)\n",
    "\n",
    "Objetivo: construir un flujo reproducible que implemente RAG sobre la guía proporcionada, mantenga diálogo multiturno y realice al menos una llamada de función get_weather(fecha) validada con Pydantic.\n",
    "\n",
    "Instrucciones rápidas:\n",
    "- Instalar dependencias: pip install -r requirements.txt.\n",
    "- (Opcional) Definir OPENAI_API_KEY como variable de entorno para usar embeddings reales.\n",
    "- Ejecutar celdas en orden desde el principio.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1) Import y configuración\n",
    "Importamos las funciones reutilizables desde src.rag_tools. Estas implementan extracción de PDF, chunking, embeddings (fallback si no hay API), construcción de índice FAISS y la función get_weather.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "from src.rag_tools import (\n",
    "    extract_text_from_pdf,\n",
    "    chunk_text,\n",
    "    get_embeddings,\n",
    "    build_faiss_index,\n",
    "    save_vectors_and_chunks,\n",
    "    save_faiss_index,\n",
    "    get_weather\n",
    ")\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    ""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2) Extracción y chunking\n",
    "Extraemos el texto del PDF de la guía y lo dividimos en trozos (chunks). Ajusta chunk_size y overlap si quieres otro granularidad.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "DATA = Path('data') / 'TENERIFE.pdf'\n",
    "text = extract_text_from_pdf(str(DATA))\n",
    "print('Extracted chars:', len(text))\n",
    "chunks = chunk_text(text, chunk_size=500, overlap=100)\n",
    "print('Num chunks:', len(chunks))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3) Embeddings\n",
    "Calculamos embeddings para cada chunk. Si OPENAI_API_KEY está definida, se usan embeddings de OpenAI; si no, se usa un embedding de respaldo determinista para reproducibilidad.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "vectors = get_embeddings(chunks)\n",
    "print('Embeddings shape:', vectors.shape)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4) Construcción del índice (FAISS si está disponible)\n",
    "Intentamos construir y guardar un índice FAISS; si no está disponible, se mantiene el fallback por fuerza bruta (vectores + búsqueda coseno).\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Intentar construir FAISS\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    index = build_faiss_index(vectors)\n",
    "    print('FAISS index built')\n",
    "    use_faiss = True\n",
    "except Exception as e:\n",
    "    print('FAISS not available, will use brute-force search:', e)\n",
    "    index = None\n",
    "    use_faiss = False\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5) Persistencia del índice y datos\n",
    "Guardamos ectors.npy y chunks.json en rtifacts/tenerife_index/. Si FAISS está disponible, también guardamos el fichero del índice.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "ART = Path('artifacts') / 'tenerife_index'\n",
    "ART.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "save_vectors_and_chunks(vectors, chunks, str(ART))\n",
    "if use_faiss and index is not None:\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        save_faiss_index(index, str(ART / 'faiss.index'))\n",
    "        print('Index saved to', ART)\n",
    "    except Exception as e:\n",
    "        print('Error saving FAISS index:', e)\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('FAISS not used; vectors and chunks saved for brute-force fallback')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6) Ejecuciones de la función get_weather\n",
    "Ejecutamos get_weather al menos tres veces (requisito del enunciado). Las llamadas se registran en logs/weather.log.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "for d in ['2026-01-14', '2026-01-15', '2026-01-16']:\n",
    "    print(d, get_weather(d))\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7) Evaluación rápida: histogramas de similitud y visualización de resultados\n",
    "Tomamos algunos ejemplos de query, calculamos embeddings y mostramos la distribución de similitud. También mostramos los top chunks recuperados.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "qs = [\n",
    "    'mejores playas para familias',\n",
    "    'senderismo en el norte de Tenerife',\n",
    "    'restaurantes tradicionales en Santa Cruz'\n",
    "]\n",
    "qvs = get_embeddings(qs)\n",
    "sims_all = []\n",
    "for qv in qvs:\n",
    "    sims = []\n",
    "    for v in vectors:\n",
    "        a = qv / (np.linalg.norm(qv) + 1e-12)\n",
    "        b = v / (np.linalg.norm(v) + 1e-12)\n",
    "        sims.append(float(np.dot(a, b)))\n",
    "    sims_all.append(sims)\n",
    "    plt.hist(sims, bins=20, alpha=0.6)\n",
    "    plt.title('Similarity distribution for query')\n",
    "    plt.show()\n",
    "for qi, sims in enumerate(sims_all):\n",
    "    top = sorted(range(len(sims)), key=lambda i: sims[i], reverse=True)[:2]\n",
    "    print('Query:', qs[qi])\n",
    "    for i in top:\n",
    "        print('-', chunks[i][:300])\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8) Evaluación reproducible: precision@k\n",
    "Calculamos precision@1, @3 y @5 para un conjunto de queries etiquetadas.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "import csv\n",
    "labels = [\n",
    "    {'query':'playas familiares en Tenerife','expect_kw':'playa'},\n",
    "    {'query':'mejor zona para surf','expect_kw':'surf'},\n",
    "    {'query':'senderos y rutas de montaña','expect_kw':'sendero'},\n",
    "    {'query':'museos en Santa Cruz','expect_kw':'museo'},\n",
    "    {'query':'dónde ver cetáceos','expect_kw':'cetáceo'},\n",
    "    {'query':'fiestas locales tradicionales','expect_kw':'fiesta'},\n",
    "    {'query':'restaurantes de cocina canaria','expect_kw':'restaurante'},\n",
    "    {'query':'transporte público en Tenerife','expect_kw':'autobús'},\n",
    "    {'query':'clima en enero','expect_kw':'clima'},\n",
    "    {'query':'actividades para niños','expect_kw':'familia'}\n",
    "]\n",
    "def retrieve_topk(q, k=5):\n",
    "    qv = get_embeddings([q])[0]\n",
    "    sims = []\n",
    "    for v in vectors:\n",
    "        a = qv / (np.linalg.norm(qv) + 1e-12)\n",
    "        b = v / (np.linalg.norm(v) + 1e-12)\n",
    "        sims.append(float(np.dot(a, b)))\n",
    "    top = sorted(range(len(sims)), key=lambda i: sims[i], reverse=True)[:k]\n",
    "    return top\n",
    "\n",
    "results = []\n",
    "for lab in labels:\n",
    "    for k in [1,3,5]:\n",
    "        top = retrieve_topk(lab['query'], k=k)\n",
    "        hit = any(lab['expect_kw'].lower() in chunks[i].lower() for i in top)\n",
    "        results.append((k, int(hit)))\n",
    "\n",
    "summary = {}\n",
    "for k in [1,3,5]:\n",
    "    vals = [v for kk, v in results if kk == k]\n",
    "    precision = sum(vals)/len(vals) if vals else 0.0\n",
    "    summary[k] = precision\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Precision@k:')\n",
    "for k, p in summary.items():\n",
    "    print(f'  @ {k}: {p:.3f}')\n",
    "outp = Path('artifacts') / 'tenerife_index' / 'metrics_precision_at_k.csv'\n",
    "outp.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "with open(outp, 'w', newline='', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n",
    "    w = csv.writer(f)\n",
    "    w.writerow(['k','precision'])\n",
    "    for k,p in summary.items():\n",
    "        w.writerow([k, p])\n",
    "print('Saved metrics to', outp)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Notas finales\n",
    "- Si quieres ejecutar con embeddings reales, define OPENAI_API_KEY antes de ejecutar el notebook.\n",
    "- No incluyas la clave en el repositorio; usa Secrets en GitHub para CI.\n",
    "- Revisa rtifacts/ y logs/ localmente; no subir artefactos binarios al repositorio (usa .gitignore).\n"
   ]
  }
 ],
